          en: 'The moment the block B battle royale begins, a group of fighters turns on [[bellamy|Bellamy]] together, and the crowd protests that this is no battle royale any more. Dagama answers that they can call him a coward once they are dead: there is only one winner, and winning is all that counts. The announcer names him as the man behind the trick. His plan is to guard [[elizabello-ii|Elizabello II]], whose King Punch can bring down a fort but takes an hour to prepare, while his hired men thin out the field; even [[tank-lepanto|Tank Lepanto]], captain of Dressrosa’s Self-Defense Army, has taken his money. Bellamy and the other dangerous ones must go first, he decides, before his own side loses too many men.',
