          en: 'While the colosseum is still roaring over block A, Gambia the Missionary, staff officer of Bartolomeo’s Barto Club, walks in on a gladiator who is taking notes and murmuring into a transponder snail. He has heard famous names on the man’s lips, his own among them, and he presses him: is he talking to himself? What is that note? Is he a Marine? The gladiator tells his caller he will ring back in ten minutes, and a moment later Gambia has stopped asking. When the call resumes, [[maynard|Maynard]], a vice admiral undercover, says the Missionary can be crossed off the list: it was not him he saw after all.',
